{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/121131-using-the-firstborn","id":121131,"title":"Using the Firstborn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-28T12:45:08-07:00","id":121131,"title":"Using the Firstborn","content":"Setting hack: the Firstborn are not some distant deities hunting in the depths of the Shadow who the average werewolf never gets to see, whose entire existence is a matter of faith.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn show up every now and then. They occasionally make their will know to the Uratha. All nine of them.<br /> <br /> If you're a PC, interesting things happen around you, and you're bound to see your tribal totem one day.<br /> <br /> They're still wolf gods, and they don't care for deus ex machina. They won't do your job or interfere in your hunts in any way. They won't save your life when the Pure are at your throats. You don't get to summon them and beg for their help like lesser spirits. The Firstborn children of Father Wolf choose when to make themselves known.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn are not nice or compassionate or human. They're spirits, and as thus, bound by their intrinsic nature. They do not know or care about human concerns or Harmony. Outside of their individual characteristics, they know only the hunt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:46:34-07:00","id":121132,"title":"","content":"Your packmate lies dead in your arms. The bitch that killed him - your OTHER packmate, the one who secretly went to the worst loci to sacrifice to the Gods of Sin - has already won. Soon the poison will kill you. And she's already coming to slaughter your family.<br /> <br /> You hear a howl. Not just any howl. The Destroyer's howl, touching you at the core of your wolf heart.<br /> <br /> Fenris can't bring back your dead packmate. The wolf that knows only destruction can't take away the pain. But he feeds your fury - makes it real, true and strong.<br /> <br /> You know what he wants you to do. It's in your blood. He has given you his strength.<br /> <br /> Bring him the Bale Hound's still beating heart.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Only you can see him as he snaps at her throat. Not even the woman herself - a Herd functionary, not even wolf-blooded, entirely blind to the world of Shadows - not even she can see the Destroyer as he circles her, daring you to tear her throat out like he wants you to.<br /> <br /> She's probably never even been in a fistfight, never been hunted by wolves before in her life; but that is of no consequence to Fenris. In her way, she has defeated and shamed the pack - stolen their territory by way of a simple court order.<br /> <br /> Offer no surrender that you would not accept. The Destroyer Wolf doesn't care about human law or concepts of morality - his pack has been shamed. He wants you to take your revenge and get your talons bloody, right this instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:59:43-07:00","id":121146,"title":"","content":"They're all dead. So are the spirits of disease and pestilence, of course - you were the one to finally figure out their weaknesses and use them against them. The Bone Shadows must be proud of you.<br /> <br /> Still too late - your pack lies calm in death.<br /> <br /> What reason is there for you to continue? It's not like you're going to live long, with the taint of disease in your blood.<br /> <br /> A white wolf snarls as you lie there bleeding. &quot;Not yet&quot;, she whispers in your ear. &quot;Not tonight&quot;. Your packmates might have joined her, but the Death Wolf still needs you to hunt in the Flesh only a little more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nobody in the pack really wants to get close to that abandoned tunnel again. Your alpha, the strongest warrior in the pack, is still in the wheelchair from the last time you've been close to that place.<br /> <br /> You've seen the Death Wolf stalk near the tunnel - always so that you could see her. Daring you to enter - to face the mysteries and dangers inside. Of course you're afraid - even your alpha admits so - but Death Wolf, the wolf who treads the darkest of places, she who faced death and came back, still needs to you go there again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:07:59-07:00","id":121154,"title":"","content":"The spiders are closing in. They clearly aren't natural - neither are you - but that doesn't matter much. This is a hunt, you're outnumbered, in unfamiliar territory, and you're their prey, and they've almost cornered you.<br /> <br /> There's a snarl. You strain your eyes as you finally see the blackest of wolves in a little hole beneath the trees. She runs. No time to think - you follow.<br /> <br /> As you lose her scent, you find yourself near a lake. Maybe you can hide here. Maybe the spiders can't find you in this place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The hunting grounds have been violated.<br /> <br /> The intruder is a wolf like you, only she wasn't lucky enough to immediately be found by a pack of Forsaken wolves after her change.<br /> <br /> The hunting grounds have been violated. It's not in the nature of the Black Wolf to make her displeasure known in words. It's also hardly necessary. She bares her fangs at the poor girl, and the pack knows what to do.<br /> <br /> Black Wolf values her tribe's purity - The People Do Not Murder The People - but she still demands vengeance, and ignorance is never an excuse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:27:06-07:00","id":121162,"title":"","content":"When you first met the Red Wolf, he came to you in the shape of a man. Baggy pants, terrible hair, - and you still knew the guy was a wolf-god who could flip out and transform into tons of raging, glorious, primordial, divine wolf-death any minute.<br /> <br /> He didn't talk to you - there was no need to do so. He only glanced up from his conversation with the local homeless - and the little knowing smile and nod he gave you was enough for you to know that the Red Wolf, the first wolf-god to ever stalk the cities, is still around, he does care about his tribe, and he'll never stop looking out for the Iron Masters, even in places where one would never expect him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:43:47-07:00","id":121168,"title":"","content":"You still get to see the Red Wolf in the shape of a man, even after the pack has been badly hurt and the Pure have turned your territory to hell. This time, however, he's grinning at you while cleaning his canine teeth with a knife.<br /> <br /> It's a dare. It's a <i>challenge</i>.<br /> <br /> Can you be flexible enough to adapt to the difficult circumstances you're in? Can you deal with your enemies with the cunning required of you as a true Iron Master?<br /> <br /> Only now you see that the knife the Red Wolf is using is of pure silver.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:56:18-07:00","id":121804,"title":"","content":"Thoughts? Ideas? Comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:41:45-07:00","id":121906,"title":"","content":"I was expecting the Winter Wolf's teaser","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:54:11-07:00","id":121919,"title":"","content":"We stumbled across two powerful, mysterious people-looking things in our chronicle. One looked at us like we were roaches (it was in a fancy restaurant) and the other seemed polite but dismissive. We never figured it out but the ST let it slip that it was a couple of the Firstborn attempting to make an agreement over something plot-related in a neutral ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:26:24-07:00","id":121943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/121131-using-the-firstborn?p=121906#post121906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting the Winter Wolf's teaser</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude!<br /> <br /> <br /> You've shamed the pack. The Forsaken have lost the 7th district to the Ivory Claws, and it's because of your indecisiveness, your failure.<br /> <br /> It is at this point that you know the Winter Wolf is watching you. He doesn't care about your past successes. You'e failed him.<br /> <br /> And now he's in this very room. He doesn't speak, doesn't even snarl at you. This god's glance is accusation enough, and as he turns his back on you and leaves, you know what to do next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As the pack is howling out its victory to the Moon, you hear a voice joining the chorus.<br /> <br /> It's not a voice, it's roar of thunder.<br /> <br /> None of the Storm Lords in the pack could miss the pride in the Winter Wolf's howl as he pays his respect to the pack's strength and resourcefulness. Neither do they miss the inherent challenge. The Winter Wolf expects to see more victories in his name.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:34:40-07:00","id":121949,"title":"","content":"When the wolf-thing stares at you, you're too scared to move. It's not like as if there was a point in moving - if it wanted you dead, your throat would already be in pieces.<br /> <br /> You don't know why it's not attacking. It shouldn't be the herd's presence - none of the stories ever told you anything about the Dire Wolf being compassionate or careful around humans.<br /> <br /> There's nothing but unending savagery in its eyes as it stares at you. &quot;My pack is hungry.&quot; - it's a growl so deep it almost stops your wolf-heart.<br /> <br /> The next thing you know, you're in the forests. Did you run there all by yourself? In the wolf form? Scaring how many humans, exactly?<br /> <br /> You're still more frightened than you've ever been in your life.<br /> <br /> That's when you hear the Predator King's howls.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:00:26-07:00","id":122010,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, this is <i>quite </i>similar to something we do in my game, where the Firstborn are a bit more involved.<br /> <br /> <u><b>What are Tribes? Who are the Firstborn and what do they do?</b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Tribes are the chosen groupings of the Werewolves -- and they look very little like human tribes, or like the Covenants, Courts, and Orders of the other supernatural nations. Werewolf tribes are essentially </span></span><i>philosophies</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">, ideological prisms through which one looks at the world. They have no offices, no hierarchy, no organization. What they </span></span><i>do</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> have are the Firstborn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">The Firstborn were other children of Father Wolf, fathered on lesser wolf-spirits. Each one is an Incarnae of significant power, and they are the patrons of the Uratha. In prehistoric times, each was somehow bested by the werewolves, and consented to serve as mentors and guides for their nephews and nieces. This is a role that they continue to fulfill to the present day.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Each of the Firstborn acts as a spirit-guide and personal mentor to every werewolf in their tribe -- these are spirits powerful enough to divide their attention a thousand-ways at any given moment. They usually appear in dreams or in visions, as whispers in the back of the head or vague intuitions. Different werewolves get differing amounts of personal attention. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">They're primarily concerned with the personal growth and harmony of each werewolf. The Firstborn try to make you a better werewolf -- or a better example of their idea of a werewolf (which differs quite a bit from Tribe to Tribe). They give advice, pose challenges, or ask questions, and generally act in whatever fashion they think will get the best results in terms of a werewolf's spiritual growth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">They are </span></span><i>not</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> leaders. The Firstborn have a kind of blind-spot, they only notice very small and very big things. In their role as personal spirit-guides, they notice </span></span><i>the werewolf</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">, and </span></span><i>only</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> the werewolf. They're concerned with spiritual growth, not acting as clue-dispensers, and seem to notice things only as they pertain to the werewolf's internal growth. In their role as Incarnae, they only notice events on a truly massive scale -- they notice WWII, and they </span></span><i>might</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> notice the Blitz if someone pointed it out to them, but anything smaller is under their radar. Plus they're spirits of immense antiquity, so they're a bit... peculiar.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">That said, the Firstborn </span></span><i>do</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> act as repositories of lore and tradition for their Tribes. They won't tell you where to find the Azlu, but they might suggest a Deed Name, or the proper way to memorialize one's ancestors. They also operate as central switchboards, so to speak, helping werewolves of the same Tribe find one another. They do not (usually) teach Gifts themselves, but can direct the werewolf towards teachers. Finally, they require each werewolf to follow a Tribal Ban, in order to maintain the Firstborn's favor. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">There are eight Firstborn.</span></span><ul><li><b>Fenris-Ur</b>, the Destroyer Wolf, patron of the Blood Talons</li> <li><b>Kamduis-Ur</b>, the Death Wolf, patron of the Bone Shadows</li> <li><b>Sagrim-Ur</b>, the Red Wolf, patron of the Iron Masters</li> <li><b>Hikaon-Ur</b>, the Black Wolf, patron of the Hunters in Darkness</li> <li><b>Skolis-Ur</b>, the Winter Wolf, patron of the Storm Lords</li> <li><b>Gurim-Ur</b>, the Burning Wolf, patron of the Fire-Touched</li> <li><b>Huzuruth-Ur</b>, the Dire Wolf, patron of the Predator Kings</li> <li><b>Hathis-Ur</b>, the Silver Wolf, patron of the Ivory Claws</li> <li>A very few legends and rumors claim that there is also <b>Viruhk-Ur</b>, the Soulless Wolf, patron of the Bale Hounds -- though this may be just speculation and Bale Hound propaganda.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:09:15-07:00","id":122018,"title":"","content":"more teasers please! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:21:30-07:00","id":122029,"title":"","content":"The tribes of the moon had just won a great war for control of your city and the pure lost major ground. Full of hubris one of your pack members howled the howl of silver wolf's failure. That's when the trouble started. Armies of spirit owls now stalk your pack day and night demanding you hand over your packmate. Members of your packs movements are always known and the pure strike when you separate. Attacking the owls seems to be useless as they vanish before a blow is struck. Oh and for some reason the local vampires seem rather annoyed at the army of spirit owls over the city. They warn you they will take matters into their own hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:42:03-07:00","id":122356,"title":"","content":"When you sleep, fever dreams show you visions of past worlds.<br /> <br /> Packs of wolves hunting a spider the size of mountains. Werewolves in the war form ruling over entire tribes of men. A rabid wolf who sits at the feet of gods, soaking up their wisdom and passing it on to his tribe.<br /> <br /> Endless forests where the wolves reign supreme, free to hunt, free to kill.<br /> <br /> Can this world be restored? Can the Fire-Touched bring back the balance between the Shadow and the Flesh?<br /> <br /> Don't the children of Rabid Wolf have some sort of tribal ban that forbids them to lie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:45:00-07:00","id":122360,"title":"","content":"It's the most beautiful thing you've ever seen - a wolf made entirely out of silver. Strength given form. No Storm Lord you know is that strong, that perfect.<br /> <br /> It's also the most beautiful, if sad thing you've ever heard. He's howling out his pain, anguish, fury and disappointment to the world. No Cahalith you know can howl that passionately and command such a presence with his voice.<br /> <br /> It's at this moment that you see who the silver wolf is howling to - it's the Mother - the divine, insane moon.<br /> <br /> The silver wolf's head turns. Red, hateful eyes gaze into your soul.<br /> <br /> And he's gone.<br /> <br /> In the next few week, the Pure double their efforts to take away your resources, hurt your people, destroy your bases of strength, hunt you down and kill you.<br /> <br /> The Silver Wolf might be able to handle being rejected by the Mother, but he certainly cannot allow anyone who has seen him in his moment of weakness to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}